 * Applies the backwards tie-break: compare the tied candidates round by
 * round from the first round counted, keeping only those with the fewest
 * votes at the first round where they are not all equal, and repeating
 * (restarting from the first round is a no-op for rounds already equal, so
 * a single forward pass suffices). If a single round of history never
 * separates them, the candidate whose name sorts last by code point is
 * chosen.
